on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/spd_campaign.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> Slips Away

Low-ranking party members loyal to Staal have steadily climbed the ranks, until a new executive committee finally replaces the old guard that had served the party since the founding of the republic.

At its head now stand Staal’s yes-men—figures like the notorious former Defense Minister Jarren Brask and Lothar Erdmann, a nationalist voice within the Greater Worker's Guild, fiercely hostile to the Treaty of Etaluxia and far closer to Staal’s ideology than the mere pragmatism of Bristol or Leighart.

The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">Commonwealth National Unity Front</span> welcomes its new member.

- @spd_joever

@spd_joever
